5 is not available in real time); they are not ranked. AtlasCRPS, FuXi and Atlas started from the IFS analysis join when all 38 starts are done.", "rainfallAI, stack v2 (statistical baseline): version chosen after scores on this same period were seen (several test looks), so these numbers are optimistic; the clean comparison is the forward table from the 2026-11-09 cycle (rainfallAI frozen 2026-11-08).", "Climatology = the 2021-2025 MRMS average for the same calendar window (valid day +-15 days) in each 0.1 deg cell (cells outside the MRMS data area filled from the nearest cell; imputation mask in rainfallAI/data/refs/imputed/); in the probability tables its probabilities (share of those 155 days reaching each amount) are the reference of the Brier skill score, so climatology scores 0 and above 0 means better than climatology (at gauges: the gauge's cell). Reference rows are shown, never ranked, and do not shape the common sample.", "Persistence = the observed MRMS (Pass 2) 24 h total ending at the start, repeated for all 7 days (probabilities from the same 1.1 deg neighbourhood as the single runs); it is published about 2 h after the start. An analysis-based reference, not an operational forecast product. Reference rows are shown, never ranked, and do not shape the common sample."], "policy": "Rows whose start is not available in real time (ERA5, which assimilates observations from after the start, or IFS starts with same-day OISST sea temperature / ERA5 clouds) are shown as an unranked reference; ranked rows share one sample; group_rank = rank within single runs / ensemble means / post-processed products", "group_labels": {"single": "single runs (raw, 1.1 deg neighbourhood)", "ensmean": "ensembles (raw, share of members)", "postproc": "post-processed on observations", "reference": "reference: start not available in real time (ERA5, or same-day OISST / ERA5 clouds; unranked)"}, "rank_metric": "bss01"}}